{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Sarai took.</b> She took her with words: \"Fortunate are you to have merited cleaving to so holy a body\" (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>At the end of ten years.</b> The fixed deadline for a woman who waited ten years and did not bear children to her husband — he is obligated to marry another." "<b>For Avram's sojourn, etc.</b> This tells that dwelling outside the Land does not count toward the reckoning (some texts read: the tally), because he was not told ״וְאֶעֶשְׂךָ לְגוֹי גָּדוֹל״ until he would come to the land of Israel."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:54.090247232Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}